// Commitments and proofs hashed via memcpy as raw bytes BEFORE G1 point validation
// G1 validation (blst_p1_uncompress + blst_p1_in_g1) occurs during compute_weighted_sum_of_commitments
// Non-G1 commitment bytes -> hashed into r, then cause C_KZG_BADARGS error return (not false-positive accept)
// Cell bytes treated as raw 4096-byte arrays with no per-field-element canonicalization

// C library: pairings_verify(&final_g1_sum, blst_p2_generator(), &proof_lincomb, &power_of_s)
// final_g1_sum = commitment_sum - interpolation_poly_commit + weighted_proof_sum (G1)
// blst_p2_generator() = [1] in G2
// power_of_s = g2_values_monomial[FIELD_ELEMENTS_PER_CELL] = [s^n] in G2
// Equivalent: e(final_g1_sum, [1]) == e(proof_lincomb, [s^n]) per EIP-7594

// r derived: blst_sha256(domain || constants || all_inputs) -> blst_scalar_from_bendian -> blst_fr_from_scalar
// SHA-256 output: 256 bits. BLS12-381 field order p ~2^254.86.
// 2^256/p ~2.2: r wraps ~2.2 times, creating ~9% non-uniformity bias
// Effective entropy: ~253 bits. Security level: 128-bit (limited by SHA-256 birthday).

